re.","what''s a beanbag? it''s a sort of furniture","what''s a beanbag it''s a sort of furniture","what''s a beanbag? — it''s a sort of furniture."]},{"id":"6","prompt":"Он похож на большую подушку.","acceptedAnswers":["It is like a big cushion.","It looks like a big cushion.","it''s like a big cushion.","It is like a big cushion","It looks like a big cushion","it’s like a big cushion.","it''s like a big cushion"]}]}}],"reference":{"version":1,"id":"a12w4l1-language-focus-homework-rule","kind":"rule-page","title":"Как описать внешний вид вещи","instruction":"Click the button next to each sentence and choose its meaning.","blocks":[{"type":"rule","title":"Как описать внешний вид вещи","text":"Когда вы хотите сказать, как выглядит вещь, используйте look / looks + прилагательное. Например, The sweater looks warm — «Свитер выглядит тёплым». Вы делитесь впечатлением по внешнему виду.\n\nЕсли вещь напоминает вам другую, используйте look / looks like + существительное или сочетание с ним: This coat looks like my old coat — «Это пальто похоже на моё старое пальто». Здесь like означает сходство, а не «нравится».\n\nСравните:\nIt looks good. — Мы описываем впечатление.\nIt looks like my coat. — Мы говорим, на что вещь похожа.\n\nФорма глагола зависит от того, о ком или о чём вы говорите:\nI / you / we / they → look\nhe / she / it → looks\n\nПоэтому об одном предмете говорим The coat looks good, а о нескольких — The coats look good.\n\nПосле like действуют знакомые правила артиклей: like a coat, like an old coat, но like my coat — перед my артикль не нужен.\n\nЧтобы спросить о внешнем впечатлении, используйте How does it look? — «Как это выглядит?» После does глагол look стоит без окончания -s.","highlights":["look / looks + прилагательное","The sweater looks warm","look / looks like + существительное или сочетание с ним","This coat looks like my old coat","like","It looks good.","It looks like my coat.","I / you / we / they → look","he / she / it → looks","The coat looks good","The coats look good","like a coat","like an old coat","like my coat","my","How does it look?","does","look","-s"]}]},"exercises":[{"version":1,"id":"L3-M02","kind":"matching","title":"Match the pictures with the words.","layout":"picture-word","items":[{"id":"L3_IMG_01","mediaRef":"L3_IMG_01","text":"Picture 1","correctId":"scarf","assetId":"L3_IMG_01","alt":"Picture 1","image":"assets/lesson-media/a1-2/module-4/lesson-3/media/scarf-cutout.webp","imageWidth":482,"imageHeight":486},{"id":"L3_IMG_02","mediaRef":"L3_IMG_02","text":"Picture 2","correctId":"belt","assetId":"L3_IMG_02","alt":"Picture 2","image":"assets/lesson-media/a1-2/module-4/lesson-3/media/belt-cutout.webp","imageWidth":494,"imageHeight":275},{"id":"L3_IMG_03","mediaRef":"L3_IMG_03","text":"Picture 3","correctId":"gloves","assetId":"L3_IMG_03","alt":"Picture 3","image":"assets/lesson-media/a1-2/module-4/lesson-3/media/gloves-cutout.webp","imageWidth":416,"imageHeight":480},{"id":"L3_IMG_04","mediaRef":"L3_IMG_04","text":"Picture 4","correctId":"cap","assetId":"L3_IMG_04","alt":"Picture 4","image":"assets/lesson-media/a1-2/module-4/lesson-3/media/cap-cutout.webp","imageWidth":501,"imageHeight":371},{"id":"L3_IMG_05","mediaRef":"L3_IMG_05","text":"Picture 5","correctId":"tie","assetId":"L3_IMG_05","alt":"Picture 5","image":"assets/lesson-media/a1-2/module-4/lesson-3/media/tie-cutout.webp","imageWidth":311,"imageHeight":488},{"id":"L3_IMG_06","mediaRef":"L3_IMG_06","text":"Picture 6","correctId":"sunglasses","assetId":"L3_IMG_06","alt":"Picture 6","image":"assets/lesson-media/a1-2/module-4/lesson-3/media/sunglasses-cutout.webp","imageWidth":522,"imageHeight":249}],"options":[{"id":"sunglasses","text":"sunglasses"},{"id":"tie","text":"tie"},{"id":"scarf","text":"scarf"},{"id":"cap","text":"cap"},{"id":"gloves","text":"gloves"},{"id":"belt","text":"belt"}]},{"version":1,"id":"L4-question-answer-match","kind":"matching","title":"Match the questions with the answers.","items":[{"id":"1","text":"What is he like?","correctId":"o0"},{"id":"2","text":"What does she look like?","correctId":"o1"},{"id":"3","text":"What does he look like?","correctId":"o2"},{"id":"4","text":"What is she like?","correctId":"o3"}],"options":[{"id":"o1","text":"Her hair is short and curly."},{"id":"o0","text":"He’s a little lazy at home."},{"id":"o3","text":"She’s helpful. She often helps me with my homework."},{"id":"o2","text":"He has long straight hair."}]},{"version":1,"id":"L5-explanation-gaps","kind":"gaps","title":"Complete the sentences.","inputMode":"text","items":[{"id":"1","segments":["This beanbag is in the living room. It’s a ",{"id":"gap1","answers":["kind","type","sort"]}," of furniture."]},{"id":"2","segments":["I’d like bubble tea, please. It’s a ",{"id":"gap2","answers":["type","kind","sort"]}," of drink."]},{"id":"3","segments":["This poncho is warm and colorful. It’s a ",{"id":"gap3","answers":["sort","kind","type"]}," of clothing."]},{"id":"4","segments":["This igloo is small. It’s ",{"id":"gap4","answers":["like"]}," a little house."]},{"id":"5","segments":["Bao is food, but it looks different from the food I usually eat. It’s a ",{"id":"gap5","answers":["type","kind","sort"]}," of food."]},{"id":"6","segments":["There is a kiosk near the park. It’s ",{"id":"gap6","answers":["like"]}," a small supermarket."]}]},{"version":1,"id":"L6-homework-1","kind":"writing","title":"Translate into English.","instruction":"Переведите на английский.","responseMode":"accepted","revealPossibleAnswers":false,"items":[{"id":"1","prompt":"Как смотрятся эти свитеры?","acceptedAnswers":["How do these sweaters look?","How do these sweaters look"]},{"id":"2","prompt":"Они действительно красивые.","acceptedAnswers":["They are really beautiful.","They are really pretty.","they''re really beautiful.","they''re really pretty.","They are really beautiful","They are really pretty","they’re really beautiful.","they''re really beautiful","they’re really pretty.","they''re really pretty"]},{"id":"3","pr